From jestabro@amt.tay1.dec.com Fri Sep  6 01:46:01 1996
Message-ID: <199609050116.VAA04540@linux03.amt.tay1.dec.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Sep 1996 21:16:23 -0400
From: jestabro@amt.tay1.dec.com <jestabro@amt.tay1.dec.com>
Subject: Re: BT-956C problems
In-Reply-To: <3232da5a.43310994@mail.eunet.ch>

>>> Francois Jaccard said:
> 
> I have problems with my Buslogic BT-956C on a Cabriolet:
> 
> It is not seen by MILO (2.0.12). It says:
> dev_config: don't know how to set hostid of SCSI device (104b:1040)
> 
> Do I need a special MILO that supports Buslogic?

Well, at least it knew it was a SCSI controller... :-)

That message is simply an artifact of when we only supported the NCR810
controller; sometimes it would be initialized in such a way that the host ID
of the controller itself was 0, not the usual 7. So now MILO tries to make
sure that *all* SCSI controllers have host ID set to 7, but it really only
knows how to do that for the NCR810... :-)

I think you just need a newer MILO, it was only recently that MILOs were
being built with BusLogic and QLogic drivers as well as the NCR810. 

--Jay++

